[Music]  we'll likely be breaking records this  week with the hot temperatures in las  vegas and it's really a lot for  anybody to handle but especially for  those who are new to the valley  oracle mana joining us now live outside  in that heat with  what some people are doing to try and  keep cool erko  well denise we all know the basics of  handling a heat wave  drink plenty of water wear light  clothing and make sure your ac  is working properly but people who've  just recently moved to las vegas  have not experienced the temperatures  that we're seeing this week  so we wanted to see how they're coping  coming to vegas  it was kind of a big shock david alcaraz  duran just moved to las vegas two months  ago  like many he sold his san francisco home  due to the hot housing market  but the weather he was used to 60 to 70  degrees on average  is definitely a far cry from the harsh  heat of the vegas valley  didn't realize that the summers were so  hot here the high temperatures this week  could break records one thing alcaraz  duran was surprised by  was how hot the inside of his car was  getting but he's already learning what  the locals do  one of my best friends actually  recommended that you get a sunshine  and put that up in the window so i never  had to have a sunshine sunshine before  but  i'm definitely going to run out to the  store and get one officials say even  those who've lived in vegas for years  still need a reminder  especially since this week's heat wave  is one for the books  for the first time my vehicle overheated  this year hasn't done it  in 10 years the best way to protect  yourself stay out of the sun  stay indoors between the hottest hours  of the day  which is about 2 p.m to 7 p.m that's  something alcaraz duran plans to do as  he settles in to his new home  we stay indoors try to stay in air  conditioning as much as possible  now for all our newer las vegas out  there we just wanted to give you some  extra tips  keep an eye on your car the heat can do  some serious damage  including sparking fires if the wires  melt so if you notice any issues get  your car checked out immediately  and do not park it in your garage also  the pavement  can get extremely hot so make sure to  walk your pets early in the morning  or late at night and you can also buy  them little slippers to make sure  that they're protected reporting live in  las vegas tonight orca mana 8 news now

